                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da0a1fad-9944-3fc0-ab49-f7db000eaa3d",
                        "entry_id": "15834dfb-648d-3740-a345-b852d4bbb84b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "три произведения одного автора, объединенных общей идеей и преемственностью сюжета"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5c56897-51b7-4773-9506-8d446ca2ec17",
                                "sense_id": "da0a1fad-9944-3fc0-ab49-f7db000eaa3d",
                                "text": "Тогда-то, должно быть, Лермонтов сообщил Белинскому свой замысел, написать романическую трилогию, три романа из трёх эпох жизни русского общества (века Екатерины II, Александра I и современной ему эпохи)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "377b29bf-bf8a-4011-ad43-bccb25bfcfc5",
                                "sense_id": "da0a1fad-9944-3fc0-ab49-f7db000eaa3d",
                                "text": "В 1954 году вышли из печати первые две книги трилогии Д. Р. Р. Толкина «Властелин колец»."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d244bbf-283e-4416-974e-d20a05851c1c",
                        "source_entry_id": "15834dfb-648d-3740-a345-b852d4bbb84b",
                        "source_sense_id": "da0a1fad-9944-3fc0-ab49-f7db000eaa3d",
                        "target_lang_word": "trilogy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trilogy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d44b697-3a47-3947-8245-eccb9f5b52bf",
                                        "entry_id": "d457db53-6014-3bce-ba97-3a79ed495394",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A set of three connected works, usually dramas, literary pieces, films, or musical compositions, all related by theme, characters, or setting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "264645fb-b9bf-46df-909d-051ffbf77f44",
                                                "sense_id": "8d44b697-3a47-3947-8245-eccb9f5b52bf",
                                                "text": "That such a safe adaptation could come of The Hunger Games speaks more to the trilogy’s commercial ascent than the book’s actual content, which is audacious and savvy in its dark calculations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "017968d7-c3ea-4a8f-8a3e-01f4557f2ce0",
                                                "sense_id": "8d44b697-3a47-3947-8245-eccb9f5b52bf",
                                                "text": "Daisy Ridley has reawakened the debate over “Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker’s” biggest reveal, saying that the character of Rey’s lineage wasn’t clear to her even partway through filming the final chapter of the trilogy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e599f78d-07c7-418e-b820-9c4ad04d7a51",
                        "source_entry_id": "15834dfb-648d-3740-a345-b852d4bbb84b",
                        "source_sense_id": "da0a1fad-9944-3fc0-ab49-f7db000eaa3d",
